# ── Filled in by you before shipping the Pi ───────────────────────────────────

# Cloudflare named tunnel token
# Steps (one-time per restaurant):
#   1. cloudflared tunnel create restaurant-name
#   2. cloudflared tunnel route dns restaurant-name print.restaurant-name.easymaz.com
#   3. cloudflared tunnel token restaurant-name  → paste below
#
# Nothing is entered in admin. The API reaches this bridge over the box's own network and knows
# where it is from its own configuration; admin has no printer address field and has not needed one
# since printing started going through the API.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# ── The register's printer — required ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Named stations below are optional; this one is not. A receipt is a fiscal document and there is
# nowhere else for it to go, so with none of these set the bridge warns at startup and every receipt
# fails against a guessed 127.0.0.1. Set exactly one of the three.

# USB via CUPS (Pi connected to printer by USB cable)
PRINTER_CMD=lp -d "TM-T20III" -o raw -

# OR USB as a raw device file, when there is no CUPS queue
# PRINTER_DEVICE=/dev/usb/lp0

# OR a printer on the network — Ethernet or Wi-Fi, they are the same thing here. Both are a TCP
# socket on port 9100 and the bridge cannot tell them apart; the only difference is how the printer
# got its address. For Wi-Fi, print the printer's self-test page to read the address it was given,
# then reserve it in the router by MAC so DHCP cannot move it and stop the till printing overnight.
# PRINTER_HOST=192.168.1.50
# PRINTER_PORT=9100

# ── More than one printer — optional ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A restaurant with one printer at the till leaves this empty and everything prints there. A site
# that makes things in more than one room names each printer, and an order splits itself: food to
# the kitchen, drinks to the bar, a folio to reception.
#
# The name is the station. It is what a menu category is tagged with in admin, matched
# case-insensitively, and an unknown station prints at the register rather than vanishing.
#
#   PRINTERS=kitchen=192.168.1.50:9100,bar=192.168.1.51,reception=192.168.1.52:9100
#
# Port is optional and defaults to 9100. Any of these may be Ethernet or Wi-Fi.
#
# Per-printer overrides, for mixing paper sizes and brands on one site:
#
#   name=host:port:width:cut:codepage
#   bar=192.168.1.51:9100:32:partial:cp437
#
# width     columns at Font A — 48 for 80 mm paper, 32 for 58 mm. Default 48.
# cut       full or partial. Default full.
# codepage  the 256-character table to select. Default cp437.
#
# So a bar running narrow 58 mm rolls while the till runs 80 mm is one line here, not a second box.
# PRINTERS=

# Defaults for the register and for any station that does not override them.
# PRINTER_WIDTH=48
# PRINTER_CUT=full

# ── The rest ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared with the API. Without it the bridge refuses every job rather than accepting one from
# anybody who can reach it — a printer that prints for the whole Wi-Fi is worse than a till that
# says printing is not set up.
PRINT_SHARED_SECRET=

# Fire the cash drawer wired into the printer's kick port at the end of a cash sale.
# CASH_DRAWER=on

PORT=3001
